# Round 20 (option B production-grade) — main branch holds source only.
# All build artefacts live under `.deploy/` and are pushed to the
# `gh-pages` branch by `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`. Neither the
# `.deploy/` working dir nor the previously-tracked `dist/` belong on
# main. `dist/` is kept gitignored even though it used to be tracked
# (untracked in the same commit that introduced `.deploy/`); a stale
# locally-built `dist/` from before the migration would now be
# silently ignored.
.deploy/
dist/

# Image source — `images/ghironda.png` is the high-resolution source
# (~1.5 MB) that `scripts/generate-images.js` reads to derive every
# deployed variant: the WebP responsive set, the AVIF LCP candidate,
# the palette PNG fallback (`ghironda-fallback.png`), and the Open
# Graph share card (`og-card.jpg`). None of the deployed HTML / meta
# tags reference `ghironda.png` directly — that reference was the
# long-standing defect fixed in Apr 2026 (og:image / twitter:image /
# Schema.org logo previously pointed at this gitignored path → every
# social-media crawler got a 404). Committing the source would inflate
# every clone by 1.5 MB without runtime benefit. Devs who need to
# regenerate the variants must place the source PNG at this path
# manually — see `scripts/generate-images.js` header for the canonical
# source location.
images/ghironda.png

